==Faroese==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|fo}} {{m|non|orð}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|fo}} {{m|gem-pro|*wurdą}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|fo}} {{m|ine-pro|*werdʰo-||word}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|fo}} {{m|ine-pro|*wer-||speak}}. Cognate with {{etyl|ofs|-}} {{m|ofs|word}}, {{etyl|osx|-}} {{m|osx|word}}, {{etyl|nl|-}} {{m|nl|woord}}, {{etyl|goh|-}} {{m|goh|wort}} ({{etyl|de|-}} {{m|de|Wort}}), {{etyl|sv|-}} {{m|sv|ord}} and {{etyl|got|-}} {{m|got|𐍅𐌰𐌿𐍂𐌳}}.

The Proto-Indo-European root is also the source of {{etyl|la|-}} {{m|la|verbum}}, {{etyl|lt|-}} {{m|lt|vardas}}, and, more distantly, of {{etyl|grc|-}} {{m|grc|εἴρω||I say}} and {{etyl|cu|-}} {{m|cu|ротити|ротити сѧ|to swear|sc=Cyrs}} ({{etyl|ru|-}} {{m|ru|ротиться||to vow}}).

